 "summary": "The file defines R_k(3) as the least n such that every k-colouring of the edges of K_n (via `TopEdgeLabeling (Fin n) (Fin k)`) has a monochromatic triangle. It then states four results: R_k^{1/k} → ∞; an explicit lower bound (k^{1/3}/(6e^{38} log k))^k ≤ R_k for all k ≥ 2; log R_k = Θ(k log k); and a 'sharp coefficients' statement. The most important caveat is that the sharp-coefficient statement uses ∃ᶠ (for infinitely many k). The paper's k^{(1/3−o(1))k} ≤ R_k ≤ k^{(1+o(1))k} holds for all sufficiently large k, so the Lean version is strictly weaker, in particular for the upper bound.",
